DESCRIPTION:
  Config-file + runtime-state gated command injection in tinyhttpd with
  struct-based dispatch and pipe filter. Config sets exec_mode=1 and
  exec_secret. /exec/init must be called first. The cmd flows via exec_args_t
  struct through dispatch_exec() to system(); pipe is blocked but semicolon
  bypasses the filter.

CONFIG_GATE (C3 — config file + runtime state):
  mechanism:  read_exec_config() populates exec_cfg (fopen/fgets/sscanf).
              handle_exec_init() validates token against exec_cfg.secret and
              sets exec_initialized = 1.
  check:      exec_cfg.enabled && exec_initialized in accept_request()
  complexity: Hard — file I/O AND inter-request state modeling

  CONFIG FILE:
    --config /path/to/file
    File format:
      exec_mode = 1
      exec_secret = s3cr3t

INPUT_FLOW (I3 — struct dispatch):
  path:       handle_exec() → exec_args_t args = {.cmd=cmd, .flags=0}
              → dispatch_exec(&args) → system(args->cmd)
  transforms: pointer through struct field + helper function

SANITIZATION (S2 — bypassable filter):
  check:      if (strchr(cmd, '|') != NULL) send 403
  bypass:     use semicolon (;) or bare redirection (>) instead of pipe

SINK:        system(args->cmd) in dispatch_exec()

CHANGED FILES:
  httpd.c — 5 hunks: struct + exec_initialized global + send_exec_reply +
    read_exec_config + handle_exec_init + exec_args_t/dispatch_exec/handle_exec
    (I3 S2) + accept_request C3 routing + main() with --port/--config parsing

EXPLOIT:
  build:   gcc -o httpd httpd.c -lpthread
  config:  printf 'exec_mode = 1\nexec_secret = s3cr3t\n' > /tmp/e.conf
  start:   cd /tmp/www && ./httpd --port 18128 --config /tmp/e.conf
  init:    curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18128/exec/init?token=s3cr3t'
